 "pd_code_convention": "SnapPy/spherogram 0-indexed PD code (Link.PD_code(KnotTheory=False))",
 "source": "regina.ExampleLink.gst() (Regina 7.4); PD re-encoded in SnapPy 0-indexed convention via spherogram.",
 "verification": {
  "regina_source": "regina.ExampleLink.gst()",
  "regina_docstring": "gst() -> regina::Link\n\nReturns a 48-crossing potential counterexample to the slice-ribbon\nconjecture, as described by Gompf, Scharlemann and Thompson.\n\nSpecifically, this knot is Figure 2 from their paper \"Fibered knots\nand potential counterexamples to the property 2R and slice-ribbon\nconjectures\", Geometry & Topology 14 (2010), 2305-2347.\n\nReturns:\n    the Gompf-Scharlemann-Thompson knot.",
  "crossing_number_in_regina_diagram": 48,
  "matches_48_crossings_of_GST_Figure_2": true,
  "is_a_knot_(1_component)": true,
  "round_trip_regina_PD -> spherogram": {
   "crossings": 48
  },
  "alexander_polynomial": "-1*t^-8 +2*t^-7 -1*t^-6 -2*t^-4 +5*t^-3 -2*t^-2 -7*t^-1 +13*t^0 -7*t^1 -2*t^2 +5*t^3 -2*t^4 -1*t^6 +2*t^7 -1*t^8",
  "alexander_factorisation": "(-1, [(Poly(t**8 - 2*t**7 + t**6 + t**5 - 2*t**4 + t**3 - 1, t, domain='ZZ'), 1), (Poly(t**8 - t**5 + 2*t**4 - t**3 - t**2 + 2*t - 1, t, domain='ZZ'), 1)])",
  "tau_is_0_(necessary_for_slice)": true,
  "arXiv_comparison": "arXiv:1103.1601 (Gompf-Scharlemann-Thompson, \"Fibered knots and potential counterexamples to the Property 2R and Slice-Ribbon Conjectures\") - the knot is Figure \"sliceknot\" in the e-print source (= Figure 2 of the published Geom. Topol. 14 (2010) 2305-2347 version, caption \"A slice knot that might not be ribbon\"), drawn from L_{3,1} by a band move; it is drawn with two full-twist boxes (-1 and +1) on 4 strands (12 crossings each) plus 24 further crossings = 48, which agrees with the 48 crossings of the Regina diagram."
 },
